    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36f25452_068b2e40",
        "filename": "microdroid/fstab.microdroid",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-05T11:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The /dev/block/by-name/ symlinks are created by the userspace. The first_stage_init has the following boot flow:\n\n1. Read the fstab \u0026 filter out mount points that shouldn\u0027t be mounted in first_stage_init\n2. Get the set of devices that should be for the mounts.\n3. Walk the /sys/devices and generate \"add\" uevent for every found device\n4. Handle the uevent callbacks from kernel\n5. After all required devices were generated, stop the process\n\nIn our case, we have 2 options:\n\nOption A: always generate uevents for all the devices. This will regress a boot time (which might be OK, we don\u0027t have many devices). Additionally, it will be a more involved change in first_stage_init.\n\nOption B: tell first_stage_init when we need to wait for microdroid-vendor device (this cl). While this option is uglier, it solves the problem, and unblocks engineers that depend on being able to have /vendor partition in Microdroid.\n\nI went with option B, as a temporary approach, while I work on the proper long-term solution.",
      "parentUuid": "3cba7826_664a7d83",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 4,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "4810f567ef2b1df9ea44a009d3740a44f5e0484b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
